(* F4: Bug reproduction - logical operators reject unification variables.
   checkLogicalBinaryOp lacks unification variable handling that both
   checkArithmeticBinaryOp and checkComparisonBinaryOp have.

   When myAnd has no type signature, parameters a and b get unification
   variables. The body a && b should unify those variables with bool,
   but checkLogicalBinaryOp rejects them as non-bool, causing a type error.

   This test simply compiles the program. It should succeed (exit 0).
   With the bug, the compiler exits with error code 1 due to the
   spurious type error, making this test FAIL.
*)

myAnd(a, b) = a && b
myAnd(true, false)
